<tier type="longtitle" id="frnt-lt">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="guid" value="_1851776a-5f8c-49bd-aad1-520c8c6db67e"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="frnt-lt"></attrib></parentattributes>

<block><txt break.before="1">An Act to authorise the transfer of certain land
from trustees appointed by the Governor to a body corporate; to remove certain
restrictions on the use of the land; to provide for the repeal of the <legref
jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Trades Hall
and Literary Institute Act of 1893</i></name></legref>; and for purposes
connected therewith.</txt></block></tier>
</content>


<content type="body">

<level type="clause" id="sec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a733ca57-279d-4f7e-9866-314d98a3edd6"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>1</no><heading guid="_9174a2b6-4d56-4acc-ac13-433422954584"
id="sec.1-he"><b>Name of Act</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act may be cited as the <legref jurisd="NSW"
type="act" check="unknown" refid="act-1970-054"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Trades
Hall (Transfer of Land) Act 1970</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f1a37163-aa89-404a-a5da-787d763e68f8"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>2</no><heading guid="_6912b422-10b2-412b-80bb-d156d3a005fa"
id="sec.2-he"><b>Registrar-General may register certain memorandum of
transfer</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.2-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_32d0cb72-50f6-41fb-88ea-c874adebc786"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The persons specified in a certificate furnished
by the Minister for the purposes of this section shall be deemed to have full
power and authority to transfer to The Trades and Industrial Hall and Literary
Institute Association of Sydney Limited the land described in the Schedule to
this Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.2-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_10630916-9123-47e3-acf3-6157e90d4b25"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Where a memorandum of transfer of the land
described in the Schedule to this Act to The Trades and Industrial Hall and
Literary Institute Association of Sydney Limited is lodged with the
Registrar-General for registration, the Registrar-General shall not be
concerned to enquire whether, or be affected by notice of the fact
that:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_9df1bbf7-8391-4909-87ae-6cdb2c775305" id="sec.2-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the memorandum of transfer is required to be
executed by any person in lieu of the persons specified in a certificate
furnished by the Minister pursuant to subsection one of this
section,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_0ec987c4-c4d9-488f-9a35-7f5f7e9aa653" id="sec.2-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the memorandum of transfer is a dealing the
registration of which is prohibited by caveat number 377701, caveat number
535255 or caveat number B379304,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_8ab052d9-1d21-4a46-a01f-d7846b84b83d" id="sec.2-ssec.2-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">any case has arisen for forfeiture, reverter or
reentry in respect of the land comprised in certificate of title volume 2619
folio 69, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_ca880d17-2054-40b3-b4a0-b26de640e87a" id="sec.2-ssec.2-para1.d">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the memorandum of transfer is a dealing in breach
of any trust, condition, proviso or reservation (not being a reservation of
minerals) created or imposed by grant from the Crown volume 761 folio
123,</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">and may register the memorandum of transfer
notwithstanding any such notice.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_fdda8ad2-131d-48d8-9353-a37fa56d556e"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>3</no><heading guid="_ce325149-b6f6-4685-9b38-d1b7bdb2639e"
id="sec.3-he"><b>Dissolution of certain trusts etc</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The registration of a memorandum of transfer
under section two of this Act shall operate:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_eb674947-0ca2-4272-9334-24959fc78f27" id="sec.3-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to dissolve the trusts protected by caveat number
377701, caveat number 535255 and caveat number B379304 to the extent necessary
to authorise the Registrar-General to withdraw those caveats,
and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_657c0d2d-f719-4c59-8d86-ae0ac7ad63dd" id="sec.3-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to dissolve, revoke and annul any trusts,
conditions, provisos, reservations (other than reservations of minerals),
rights of reverter, restrictions on alienation and provisions for the
appointment of trustees arising under, contained in or imposed by grant from
the Crown volume 761 folio 123.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e7296c4c-da03-4b0c-8eef-41824268c739"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>4</no><heading guid="_1aa19817-8358-46d6-917c-2ad019500780"
id="sec.4-he"><b>Restriction on transfer of certain land</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A transfer by The Trades and Industrial Hall and
Literary Institute Association of Sydney Limited of the land comprised in
certificate of title volume 2619 folio 69 shall be void and of no effect
unless the Minister consents thereto.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_63071bee-3f47-4c0d-afb8-fa957eea0c2a"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>5</no><heading guid="_c3c6e3bf-96f9-44cd-99fc-6c46a3c640c2"
id="sec.5-he"><b>Recordings by Registrar-General</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Registrar-General may, on the registration of
a memorandum of transfer under section two of this Act, make such recordings
in the register kept by him under the <legref jurisd="NSW" type="act"
check="unknown" refid="act-1900-025"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Real Property Act
1900</i></name></legref> as to him seem necessary or convenient in consequence
of the enactment of this Act and in consequence of that registration, and may
make any recording with respect to the effect of paragraph (b) of section
three, or of section four, of this Act by reference to this
Act.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f2b636a8-3e20-419f-90c9-11bdab7c58e6"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>6</no><heading guid="_27d1ebef-5f05-456c-a8e8-299a01ae136f"
id="sec.6-he"><b>Stamp duty</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">No stamp duty under the <legref jurisd="NSW"
type="act" check="unknown" refid="act-1920-047"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Stamp
Duties Act 1920</i></name></legref> shall be chargeable upon a memorandum of
transfer referred to in section two of this Act.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.7">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_8581a190-ccb3-4530-8914-e755af82ca61"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>7</no><heading guid="_45346791-ff54-45e0-bdac-ce1c88adb793"
id="sec.7-he"><b>Repeal of certain Acts</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_35aca99d-bca3-4709-9aef-3aa92c1ba377"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The <legref jurisd="NSW" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Trades Hall and Literary Institute Act
of 1893</i></name></legref> and the <legref jurisd="NSW" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Trades Hall and Literary Institute
(Amendment) Act 1916</i></name></legref> are hereby
repealed.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_84d4c63a-a64d-4454-a225-fa901f3e61dd"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Subsection one of this section shall commence
upon a day to be appointed by the Governor and notified by proclamation
published in the Gazette, being a day that is not earlier than the day on
which a memorandum of transfer under section two of this Act is
registered.</txt></block></tier>
</level>
</content>


<content type="schedules">

<level type="schedule" id="sch">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="type" value="schedule"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_80fbe7e1-26c8-40f1-b97d-3a1028b89a34"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sch"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Schedule</b></no></head>
<block align="right" type="sourceref"><txt>(Section 2)</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1">All those pieces or parcels of land situate in
the city of Sydney parish of St. Andrew and county of Cumberland being the
whole of the land comprised in certificates of title volume 1436 folio 232,
volume 1986 folio 103, volume 2619 folio 69 and volume 3906 folio
123.</txt></block></level>
</content>


